map.某规划区常住人口 50000 人，总用地 500 ha，其中居住用地 250 h:
A planning district with 50000 residents, total land use 500 ha, of which 250 ha is residential land:
Gross population density = 50000 / 500 = 100 persons/ha;
Net population density = 50000 / 250 = 200 persons/ha;
Per-capita land use = 500 × 10000 / 50000 = 100 m² per person (new city standard 85–105, compliant).

map.用地 100 ha，目标人均 100 m²/人，居住用地占比 50%（50 ha:
Land use 100 ha, target 100 m² per person, residential land share 50% (50 ha), target net density 600 persons/ha:
Capacity by per-capita land use = 100 × 10000 / 100 = 10000 persons;
Capacity by net density = 50 × 600 = 30000 persons;
Appropriate population capacity = min(10000, 30000) = 10000 persons (constrained by per-capita land use, actual 100 m² per person).
